  {
   "id": "hello",
   "title": "Hello",
   "zh": "你好",
   "topic": "Daily life: interaction, polite behaviour (交往)",
   "notes": [
    "Chinese has two words for \"you\": 你 nǐ, for friends and people your own age, and 您 nín, a polite \"you\" for elders, teachers and people you want to show respect to. 您好 is a respectful hello.",
    "In class, students greet their teacher together with 老师好! (\"hello, teacher\"). Among friends a greeting is often simply the other person's name."
   ],
